WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.070
A long conveyor belt runs
at a perfectly steady speed.

2
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:07.200
Sand pours down onto
it from a hopper above,

3
00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:10.240
landing with no sideways
motion of its own.

4
00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:12.780
Friction in the rollers is negligible.

5
00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:15.340
The belt's speed never changes.

6
00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:18.250
So why must its motor keep pushing?

7
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.420
In this mission, you'll find the impulse
from a force that changes from moment

8
00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:23.570
to moment.

9
00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:26.680
Then you'll take a momentum
that changes with time,

10
00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:30.150
differentiate it, and get
the force straight out.

11
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:33.980
Your mission: explain why
the motor must keep pushing,

12
00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:35.630
even at a steady speed.
